0007: # concepts:
0008: # symmetry, occlusion
0009: 
0010: # description:
0011: # In the input you will see a left-right symmetric monochromatic object occluded by a colored rectangle
0012: # To make the output, remove the colored rectangle and fill in the missing parts of the object to make it left-right symmetric
0013: 
0014: def main(input_grid):
0015:     """
0016:     Remove a filled rectangular occluder and mirror the remaining object to restore symmetry.
0017: 
0018:     Input structure:
0019:     - A black grid contains a monochromatic object with left-right mirror symmetry.
0020:     - A different-colored filled rectangle overlaps and hides part of that object.
0021:     - The rectangle is itself a solid connected component.
0022: 
0023:     Rule:
0024:     - Detect the solid rectangle component and erase it to black.
0025:     - Detect mirror symmetry while ignoring the rectangle color.
0026:     - Reflect every remaining object pixel across the detected mirror axes to fill the missing cells.
0027: 
0028:     Key insight:
0029:     - The occluder color should be ignored for symmetry detection, while black remains meaningful absence.
0030:     """
0031:     # Plan:
0032:     # 1. Extract and separate the rectangle from the symmetric object
0033:     # 2. Find the left-right symmetry
0034:     # 3. Fill in the missing parts of the object
0035: 
0036:     background_color = Color.BLACK
0037: 
0038:     # Each object has a different color, so we can look at connected components by color
0039:     objects = detect_objects(input_grid, monochromatic=True, connectivity=8, background=background_color)
0040:     sprites = []
0041:     for obj in objects:
0042:         _b = bbox(obj != background_color)
0043:         if _b is None:
0044:             continue
0045:         sprites.append(crop_bbox(obj, _b))
0046:     # Find the rectangle
0047:     for obj, sprite in zip(objects, sprites):
0048:         # the rectangle will be completely filled, so we can check if its total area is the whole rectangular region
0049:         if sprite.shape[0] * sprite.shape[1] == np.sum(sprite != Color.BLACK):
