0024:     Rule:
0025:     - Detect both objects and identify the one with both mirror axes.
0026:     - Use those axes as symmetries for the whole output grid.
0027:     - For every pixel of the other object, paint all reflected orbit positions with its color.
0028: 
0029:     Key insight:
0030:     - The symmetric object defines the reflection axes; the non-symmetric object supplies
0031:       the pixels to replicate.
0032:     """
0033:     # Plan:
0034:     # 1. Detect the pair of objects and divide them by whether or not they are already symmetric
0035:     # 2. Reflect the non-symmetric object across the axes of symmetry of the symmetric object
